# Ideas files

`.cursor/ideas/` holds **ideas** docs: architecture explorations, option spaces, wild proposals. They frame thinking; they are not specs to implement.

When creating or editing `.cursor/ideas/`:

- **Options, not commitments.** Mark speculative items clearly. Do not write them as if shipped or as a todo list.
- **Not plans.** Actionable unfinished work belongs in `.cursor/plans/`. Promoting an idea means opening or updating a plan — do not turn the ideas file into a backlog.
- **Not rules.** Shipped invariants belong in `.cursor/rules/<topic>.mdc`. Ideas may link to rules for grounding; do not duplicate those write-ups here.
- **Stay useful.** Keep the decision frame (constraints, tests, trade-offs) current when the project’s real boundaries change; prune ideas that are no longer relevant.
